id: L-2026-10-18-builder-162752-001
type: insight
timestamp: '2026-10-18T16:27:52.205Z'
author: builder
title: 'Decision: approve does not take contentHash in v1 because it would move clientApiId'
summary: Reviewer C4 asked to send contentHash in approve. The broker's APPROVE_KEYS is closed and approve's params are in the VERBS descriptor hashed into clientApiId, so adding contentHash would move clientApiId; stopped per the coordinator's rule. The GUI keys its verified-action cache by (cardId, contentHash) instead, and decisionSig already binds card.contentHash kernel-side.
symbols_touched:
  - '#gui'
  - '#approval-broker'
files_modified:
  - packages/gnomon-gui/src/ui/app.ts
commit: 673456ae
learnings:
  - 'Check the descriptor before treating a param as additive: a closed param list in clientApiId makes it a v2-class change'
  - decisionSig over cardId+decision+contentHash+approver already prevents approving a stale card body
tags:
  - decision
  - gnomon
  - m1-10
  - c4
  - client-api
body: M1.10 made no change to broker/card.ts or broker.ts, so the parallel T-015 edits to card.ts (sanitizeLine, presence summary) merge cleanly. A future contentHash? param needs a planned descriptor change and clientApiId move owned by the contracts lane.
